Rule 1 (input tensors to logaddexp must have the same shape if they are not scalars)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ ∀i ∈ [1, ndim(v_1) -1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 2 (the output tensor, if provided, must have the same dtype as the input tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensors must have compatible dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10)
>>
Rule 4 (if out is specified, it should have the same shape as the input tensors after broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i)) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_3, i)) else shape(v_1,0) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 5 (If one input is a scalar and the other is a tensor, the output should have the same shape and dtype as the tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) else if ndim(v_2) = 0 then (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 6 (The out argument, if provided, must be a tensor.)
{v_3 : tensor ⊎ int ⊎ float ⊎ bool ⊎ dtype ⊎ str ⊎ list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= if v_3 = v_3 then true else false
>>
Rule 7 (If both input tensors are 0-dimensional, the output tensor, if provided, must also be 0-dimensional.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 0 then ndim(v_3) = 0
>>
Rule 8 (If out is specified, the output tensor must have a floating point or complex dtype)
{v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 10
>>
Rule 9 (If input tensors are boolean, the result should also be boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 0 then dtype_(v_3) = 0
>>
Rule 10 (If one of input tensors is complex, out tensor should be complex too)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10 then dtype_(v_3) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 10
>>
Rule 11 (Input tensors cannot be bool type. Because when input is boolean, after calculating pointwise log(exp(x)+exp(y)), it is not boolean anymore. )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 12 (If either input tensors has integer dtype, both should be converted to float. So, out tensor has floating point type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5) then (6 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 8)
>>
Rule 13 (logaddexp does not support string type tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 14 (If two input tensors are different dtypes, the lower precision tensor should be promoted to the higher precision one, resulting in out tensor having the higher precision dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) < dtype_(v_2) then dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2) else if dtype_(v_2) < dtype_(v_1) then dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) else dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 15 (If one of the input tensor is np.dtype, it should raise error.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 16 (logaddexp does not support integer input tensors, at least one of the tensors should be floating point)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8) ∨ (9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10) ∨ (9 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 17 (If out tensor is provided, then ndim of input tensors should be greater or equal to that of out tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_3) ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ ndim(v_3)
